# The app's pages and scripts always keep LF line endings, on every checkout (Windows too). The browser hashes inline scripts with
# LF line endings, so a CRLF copy would get CSP hashes that never match and the page's code would be blocked.
*.html text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
